{%- comment -%} FAQ {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="arg-faq">
  <div class="arg-faq-inner">
    <div class="arg-faq-hdr">
      <span class="arg-sec-label">Common Questions</span>
      <div class="arg-sec-title">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="arg-faq-item open"><div class="arg-faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.arg-faq-item').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="arg-faq-q-text">What is the difference between Rashi and Sun sign?</span><span class="arg-faq-arrow">+</span></div><div class="arg-faq-a"><p>In Vedic astrology, your Rashi is determined by the position of the Moon at birth, while in Western astrology the focus is on the Sun sign. Vedic astrology gives more importance to the Moon sign as it reflects your mind, emotions and inner nature — the Moon changes signs every 2–2.5 days, making the Rashi more personal and precise than the Sun sign which stays in one sign for a full month.</p></div></div>
    <div class="arg-faq-item"><div class="arg-faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.arg-faq-item').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="arg-faq-q-text">Can my Rashi change over time?</span><span class="arg-faq-arrow">+</span></div><div class="arg-faq-a"><p>No — your Rashi is fixed at birth based on the Moon's position at that exact moment. It never changes throughout your lifetime. However, the effects of your Rashi change based on which planetary periods (Dasha) are active at a given time.</p></div></div>
    <div class="arg-faq-item"><div class="arg-faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.arg-faq-item').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="arg-faq-q-text">How does knowing my Rashi help me?</span><span class="arg-faq-arrow">+</span></div><div class="arg-faq-a"><p>Knowing your Rashi helps you understand your natural personality traits, emotional patterns, compatible gemstones, lucky colours and directions, ideal career fields, compatible partners and the best timing for major life decisions. It is the foundation of your complete Vedic birth chart analysis.</p></div></div>
    <div class="arg-faq-item"><div class="arg-faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.arg-faq-item').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="arg-faq-q-text">What is the significance of Nakshatras?</span><span class="arg-faq-arrow">+</span></div><div class="arg-faq-a"><p>Nakshatras are the 27 lunar mansions that divide the zodiac into finer segments of 13 degrees 20 minutes each. Your birth Nakshatra (Janma Nakshatra) gives a much more detailed personality reading than the Rashi alone. It also determines your Vimshottari Dasha period and is used in marriage matching (Kundali Milan).</p></div></div>
    <div class="arg-faq-item"><div class="arg-faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.arg-faq-item').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="arg-faq-q-text">Is Rashi compatibility the only factor for marriage matching?</span><span class="arg-faq-arrow">+</span></div><div class="arg-faq-a"><p>No. Vedic marriage compatibility uses the Ashtakoot Guna Milan system with 8 different factors (Varna, Vashya, Tara, Yoni, Graha Maitri, Gana, Bhakut, Nadi) that together give a score out of 36. A score above 18 is considered acceptable and above 24 is good. Rashi is just one of many factors considered.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

